\ exit the caller if there is nothing to do     : cmove     ( a1 a2 n -- )  3parms >r b! a! |inst @a+ !b+ unext ;               \ move cells or slices (note address types)     : cmove>    ( a1 a2 n -- )  3parms dup >r chars+  swap r@ chars+ ( a1 a2 | n )  \ move bytes forward by small offset                begin  char- swap char- swap  dup a! over b! @a !b  next  2drop ;                                                           : -trailing ( a len -- a' len' )                                                \ trim trailing blank bytes                         >r 8 bit dup r> chars+  ( a0 a1 )                                           \ convert to byte addresses                         begin 2dup xor while                                                                                                                char- dup @  32 xor  if  over bytespan  1+ exit  then                   \ seek backward for nonblank                        repeat  dup xor ;       ( a' 0 )                                                                                            : fill      ( ca u c -- )   3parms swap >r swap a! |inst  dup !a+ unext drop ;  \ fill u cells or slices with c                 : blank     ( ca u -- )     32 fill ;                                           \ fill u chars with spaces                      -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Numeric output ______________________________________________ 10/9/26 BNE )                                                   _udata variable hld                                                             \ position of the last held char in numbuf      create numbuf 10 allot                                                          \ pictured numeric output buffer, 40 bytes      : <#        ( ud -- ud )    40  hld ! ;                                         \ start numeric conversion                      : #>        ( ud -- ca u )  2drop  numbuf hld @ tuck chars+  swap negate 40 + ; \ end numeric conversion                        : hold      ( c -- )        hld a! @a 1-  dup 0< -17 and yeet  dup !a           \ append c to the numeric conversion buffer                                 numbuf swap chars+ ! ;                              \ yeet -17 if the buffer overflows              : #         ( ud1 -- ud2 )  base @ mu/mod rot digit hold ;                      \ append next digit                             : #s        ( ud -- 0 )     begin # 2dup or 0= until ;                          \ append remaining digits                       : sign      ( n -- )        -if [char] - hold exit then drop ;                  \ append minus sign if negative                 : s.r       ( ca u width -- ) over - spaces type ;                              \ type a string right-justified in width        : d.r       ( d width -- )  >r dup >r dabs  <# #s r> sign #> r> s.r ;           \ signed double with width                      : u.r       ( u width -- )  0 swap d.r ;                                        \ unsigned with width                           : .r        ( n width -- )  >r s>d r> d.r ;                                     \ signed with width                             : d.        ( d -- )        0 d.r space ;                                       \ signed double                                 : u.        ( u -- )        0 d. ;                                              \ unsigned                                      -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Search order ________________________________________________ 10/10/26 BNE )                                                  : definitions ( -- )        context @ current ! ;                               \ compile into the first context wordlist       : contexts  ( -- n )        0 context begin @+ 128 and 0=                       \ number of wordlists in the search order                                   while swap 1+ swap repeat drop ;                                                                    : previous  ( -- )          contexts 1parm >r context dup slice+                \ drop the first wordlist of the search order                               swap r> cmove ;                                                                                     : also      ( -- )          context dup slice+  contexts 1+ cmove>              \ duplicate top of context stack                                            255  [ context |context| chars+ ] literal  ! ;      \ backstop the terminator                       : vocabulary ( <name> -- )  _text align create wordlist , does> @ context ! ;   \ create a new vocabulary                       : _contexts ( -- )          context contexts 2parms for @+ .wid next drop ;     \ list contexts with first on the left          : order     ( -- )          ." Context: " _contexts cr                          \ list the search order                                                     ." Current: " current @ .wid ;                                                                                                                                                                                                      -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             